    "https://employment.stockton.edu/jobs/operating-engineer-1-galloway-new-jersey-united-states": {
      "title": "Operating Engineer 1",
      "description": "Operating Engineer 1 - Galloway, New Jersey, United States Operating Engineer 1 - Galloway, New Jersey, United States Kiosk mode Stockton University is ranked among the top public universities in the Northeast with more than 160 undergraduate and graduate programs, as well as continuing education opportunities. Our University, one hour from Philadelphia and two hours from New York City, offers unique learning, living, and working environments throughout southern New Jersey, including the 1,600-acre Galloway campus in the Pinelands National Reserve and Atlantic City campus, located in the University District, just steps from the beach and iconic Atlantic City Boardwalk. Additional locations include Hammonton and Manahawkin. As a public University, Stockton University provides an environment for excellence to our student body through an interdisciplinary approach to liberal arts, sciences, and professional education. Founded in 1969, our University held its first classes in 1971. Our University’s welcoming and vibrant community makes Stockton a great place to learn, live, and work! Learn more about the many reasons to choose Stockton at www.Stockton.edu . Our Faculty and Staff are committed to supporting Stockton University’s strong student-centered vision and mission. Operating Engineer 1 Galloway, New Jersey Facilities & Plant Operations Staff Full-time Opened on: Oct 14 2026 Campus Location: Main Campus (Galloway) Department: Facilities & Plant Operations Salary Range: $52,308.32 - 59,402.09 Salary Information: Based on NJ Civil Service Commission regulations and is accompanied by an extremely competitive University benefits package University Pensions & Benefits Information Webpage Work Hours: Shift varies and can include weekends Brief Job Overview/Summary Under supervision of a supervisor in a state institution, department, or agency, takes a leading part in the operation and maintenance of power and heating plants and auxiliary equipment; does related work as required. Descriptions of Essential Duties/Responsibilities: • Operates, monitors, and maintains boilers, engines, turbines, motors, generators, pumps, and related auxiliary equipment to ensure safe, reliable, and efficient operation of power and heating systems • Performs routine, minor, and emergency repairs and adjustments to generators, motors, feed and vacuum pumps, blowers, governors, automatic stokes, piping, and other power plant equipment • Conducts operational tests, inspections, and readings of fuel consumption, water usage, pressure, draft conditions, temperatures, steam flow, and other system conditions; identifies abnormalities and takes appropriate corrective action • Maintains accurate operational records and inventories, including power plant logs, equipment readings, fuel and water consumption, maintenance activities, materials, supplies, and equipment usage; reports excessive consumption or operating concerns • Responds to emergencies and equipment failures ensuring the maintenance of safe and efficient operations • Knowledge of power and heating plant equipment, including various types of boilers, engines, motors, generators, pumps, governors, blowers, automatic stokers, and auxiliary equipment, as well as their proper operation, adjustment, lubrication, cleaning, maintenance, and minor repair Knowledge of safe operating practices and procedures, including the proper inspection, testing, and use of safety devices and equipment to ensure the safe and reliable operation of boilers, electrical generating equipment, and related machinery • Completes other duties as assigned Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: • Knowledge of power and heating plant equipment, including boilers, engines, motors, generators, pumps, blowers, governors, automatic stokers, and related auxiliary equipment, and their operation, adjustment, lubrication, maintenance, and minor repair • Knowledge of the methods used to operate, inspect, maintain, adjust, lubricate, clean, and perform minor repairs on power plant equipment, including generators, motors, pumps, governors, blowers, conveyors, and automatic stokers • Knowledge of safety devices, safe operating practices, and regulatory requirements applicable to power and heating plant operations and associated equipment • Knowledge of the methods used to conduct operational tests and record readings related to fuel consumption, pressure, draft conditions, temperature, steam flow, and other operating system conditions • Ability to identify, analyze, and resolve power and heating plant operational and maintenance problems • Ability to operate, maintain, and perform minor and emergency repairs on boilers, electrical generating equipment, and related power plant machinery • Ability to safely perform assigned work and maintain effective working relationships with supervisors, coworkers, contractors, and other campus personnel • Ability to prepare, maintain, and accurately document operational records, reports, inventories, equipment readings, and fuel consumption data • Ability to read, write, speak, understand, or communicate effectively Required Qualifications: • Two years of experience in work involving the operation and repair of stationary steam boilers and auxiliary equipment of a power plant or high-pressure heating plant • Must possess an appropriate Operating Engineer’s license Blue Seal refrigeration non-toxic of the appropriate grade, issued by the NJ Department of Labor • Candidates will be admitted to the examination who possess any grade Operating Engineer's license, but appointments to specific vacancies will be contingent upon possession of the appropriate license for the size and type equipment involved • Appointees will be required to possess a driver's license valid in New Jersey only if the operation of a vehicle, rather than mobility, is necessary to perform the essential duties of the positions. Screening Information: Screening of applications begins immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Applications received by (insert date below in Job Posting after clicking Generate Description) will receive full consideration. How to Apply: To apply please visit https://employment.stockton.edu or click the \"Apply\" button. Application Requirements: Individuals who apply must complete the online application, provide names and contact information for three professional references, and submit the following required documents electronically in a Microsoft Word or PDF format: Letter of Interest/Cover Letter Describing Qualifications and Accomplishments Current Resume Important: Individuals who apply must meet all Required Qualifications within the job advertisement to be considered for this position. Please note that any offer of employment is subject to, and contingent upon, completion of the University’s mandatory and favorable background check, which may include a consumer report, availability and receipt of appropriations from the State of New Jersey, and receipt of any required approvals by the University. SAME Program: In accordance with P.L. 2021, c. 465 and P.L. 2021, 466, the SAME Program permits eligible New Jersey State agencies and employers to consider qualified applicants for certain non-competitive and unclassified titles within the State workforce. Applicants seeking consideration under the New Jersey SAME Program, must indicate that status when completing the online application. You must also submit the required SAME Program documentation for this specific position, as directed by the New Jersey Civil Service Commission, in addition to all required electronic documents for this position (e.g., cover letter, resume/vita/curriculum vitae, unofficial transcripts) on or before the closing date indicated above. Individuals who apply through the SAME Program must meet all Required Qualifications within the job advertisement to be considered for this position. For more information on the SAME Program, please contact the New Jersey Civil Service Commission by emailing SAME@csc.nj.gov . Please Be Advised : Stockton University is committed to providing every University employee and prospective University employee with a work environment free from prohibited discrimination or harassment. Prohibited discrimination or harassment undermines the integrity of the employment relationship, compromises equal employment opportunity, debilitates morale, and interferes with work productivity. Stockton University will not tolerate discrimination or harassment by anyone in our workplace including supervisors, co-workers, or persons doing business with our University. Stockton University is also committed to providing a learning, living, and working environment free from sexual misconduct. Sexual misconduct is a form of prohibited conduct that may constitute sex discrimination under Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, Titles IV and VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, the New Jersey Law Against Discrimination, and other applicable federal, state, and local laws, depending on the nature of the conduct and circumstances. To report concerns related to Discrimination, Harassment, and/or Sexual Misconduct/Title IX, please contact Joshua Hayes (Director of Title VI, Title VII & Title IX Coordinator – Office of Human Resources) via email at Joshua.Hayes@stockton.edu or by phone at (609) 652-4733. Persons with disabilities, who need reasonable accommodations to participate in the application and/or selection process, may contact Bart Musitano (ADA Coordinator and Manager for University Pensions and Benefits – Office of Human Resources) via email at Bart.Musitano@stockton.edu or by phone at (609) 652-4384. In accordance with the New Jersey First Act, P.L. 2011, c. 70, effective September 1, 2011, new public employees are required to establish New Jersey residency within one year of employment, unless they qualify for an applicable statutory or University-reported exemption. Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Campus Safety Act (Clery Act), prospective employees may access Stockton’s Annual Security and Fire Safety Report (ASFSR) at https://www.stockton.edu/police/crime-statistics.html . The ASFSR contains the previous three years of reported Clery Act crime statistics, fire safety information, and information regarding campus and personal safety. Paper copies of the report are available at our Stockton University Police Department located at 101 Vera King Farris Drive in Galloway, NJ - Building 70. To request a copy of the report be sent via postal mail, please send an email to campus.police@stockton.edu or call (609) 652-4390. Apply now! Sign up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 85b10120 Last Name (required) ec7bc418 Email (required) 1ec8eb13 Job Alert 041b3607 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Facilities & Plant Operations Facilities & Plant Operations Locations Galloway, New Jersey, United States Galloway, New Jersey, United States Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Share this job with a friend! First Name (required) 8c5f69af Last Name (required) a8a4a0fa Email (required) ab8558f4 Share now Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you - we've sent an email with job to the person you entered. Content missing Office of the President Read Stockton Now Media Resources Do Business With Stockton University Alerts Bookstore Library Employment Safety Information Statements & Policies Additional Locations Atlantic City Hammonton Manahawkin Stockton University 101 Vera King Farris Drive Galloway, NJ 08205-9441 (609) 652-1776 Maps, Directions & Parking Accessibility Statement Facebook Twitter YouTube Instagram LinkedIn Flickr Snapchat TikTok Stockton University is an Equal Opportunity Institution © 2022 Stockton University Candidate Details P