    "https://employment.stockton.edu/jobs/professional-services-specialist-3-geospatial-team-leader-environmental-specialist-13m-port-republic-new-jersey-united-states-a1819570-23c0-41a9-b29c-2d9aed019166": {
      "title": "Professional Services Specialist 3, Geospatial Team Leader & Environmental Specialist (13M)",
      "description": "Professional Services Specialist 3, Geospatial Team Leader & Environmental Specialist (13M) - Port Republic, New Jersey, United States Professional Services Specialist 3, Geospatial Team Leader & Environmental Specialist (13M) - Port Republic, New Jersey, United States Kiosk mode Stockton University is ranked among the top public universities in the Northeast with more than 160 undergraduate and graduate programs, as well as continuing education opportunities. Our University, one hour from Philadelphia and two hours from New York City, offers unique learning, living, and working environments throughout southern New Jersey, including the 1,600-acre Galloway campus in the Pinelands National Reserve and Atlantic City campus, located in the University District, just steps from the beach and iconic Atlantic City Boardwalk. Additional locations include Hammonton and Manahawkin. As a public University, Stockton University provides an environment for excellence to our student body through an interdisciplinary approach to liberal arts, sciences, and professional education. Founded in 1969, our University held its first classes in 1971. Our University’s welcoming and vibrant community makes Stockton a great place to learn, live, and work! Learn more about the many reasons to choose Stockton at www.Stockton.edu . Our Faculty and Staff are committed to supporting Stockton University’s strong student-centered vision and mission. Professional Services Specialist 3, Geospatial Team Leader & Environmental Specialist (13M) Port Republic, New Jersey School of Natural Science & Mathematics AFT Professional Staff Opened on: Aug 4 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Campus Location: Coastal Research Center, Port Republic Department: School of Natural Sciences & Mathematics Salary: Range 21/Step 1, $66,067.40 Salary Information: NJ State employees are offered a full benefits package: medical, prescription drug, and dental coverage, paid time off, paid holidays, pension/retirement plan, supplemental retirement saving plan options, disability Insurance, and tax saving programs. University Pensions & Benefits Information Webpage Work Hours: Varies Brief Job Overview/Summary Stockton University is accepting applications for a Professional Services Specialist 3, Geospatial Team Leader & Environmental Specialist (13M). This is a Grant Funded position. The exponential growth of cutting-edge research projects combined with the onslaught of new technological capabilities within the NAMS Marine Science program as well as advances by the Coastal Research Center (CRC) has created the need for a Geospatial Team Leader & Environmental Specialist (PSS-3). The growing demand for advanced electronic mapping, spatial analysis, and collecting remotely sensed (LiDAR) and on-the-ground survey data has expanded the CRC’s grasp of New Jersey’s coastal zone research to a higher level that requires an experienced individual for guidance and supervision beyond traditional methods for evaluating coastal change. Geographical Information Systems (GIS) is an array of complex mapping, drawing and information evaluation tools combined in a map output program that allows CRC researchers to process large datasets for map display and then evaluate the character and relationships within the information. With the Interim Executive Director managing numerous projects and securing new funds with current CRC staff, there is a dire need for reestablished supervision of day-to-day geospatial operations, managing a growing number of junior staff to ensure timely and accurately completed project reports and deliverables. The Geospatial Team Leader will assist the CRC Interim Executive Director, Project Development and Implementation Specialist, and Hydrographic & Geotechnical Coordinator (Project Managers) in academic leadership and financial management of the grants and contracts obtained by the CRC. The Geospatial Team Leader may be assigned Project Management duties. The growth in technological capabilities has enhanced a multitude of research projects, especially awards including the New Jersey Beach Profile Network, the Marsh Futures Data Layer, UAV LiDAR data collection, as well as other projects. The Geospatial Team Leader will provide organization and guidance to new and existing research projects and direct junior staff so that work proceeds in the most efficient manner. The Geospatial Team Leader & Environmental Specialist (PSS-3) will answer directly to the Interim Executive Director of the Coastal Research Center and the Dean of the School of Natural Sciences and Mathematics. He/she will represent and act for the Interim Executive and Project Managers as requested. The salary is to be fully funded 100% by the Coastal Research Center’s income associated with client projects. Descriptions of Essential Duties/Responsibilities: Under the direction of the Interim Executive Director or the Project Development and Implementation Specialist, or Hydrographic & Geotechnical Coordinator: Oversee multiple research project GIS-based tasks to be certain that they are being performed and completed in a timely manner and as required. This includes organizing a team of junior staff and/or students to assist in completing the tasks. Participate in development and implementation of policies and alternative procedures to improve performance and meet objectives Consult Interim Executive Director on any unusual problems that may arise and work to resolve issues within the program while maintaining appropriate confidentiality. Work directly with the CRC Interim Executive Director and other Geospatial Analysts in identifying new research projects, generating cost estimates and securing new grant funding through federal, state, local & private sources. Undertake principal investigator (PI) duties for special research project awards and guide each segment of the project through the process of advising and working with the other employees responsible for the completion of the work on the project. Check and review the data collection methodology, the validity of that information and the means used to process it into deliverables to the clients. Work with NJ State and Federal agencies to develop Quality Assurance & Quality Control objectives under which the CRC performs selected GIS-based tasks for these agencies. Be the major source of developing public relations material, verbal and written presentations of completed work and research to various conferences, project meetings with clients and other avenues designed to generate additional project work by compiling, summarizing, and analyzing statistical and other data to make conclusions and recommendations. Attend key meetings; meet with clients and appropriate New Jersey political leaders and municipal officials. Provide requested information to those governmental officials so that they can make the best use of limited resources and focus attention on the proper issues facing the NJ coastal community. Assist with CRC field work, when needed. Required Qualifications: Master's degree in Marine Science, Environmental Studies, Geography, Data Science or related discipline GIS Certificate, or GISP (or working toward certification) Two years of coastal and LIDAR experience *NOTE: Applicants who do not possess the required education may substitute required experience on a year-for-year basis (30 credit hours is considered one year of college.) A Ph.D. or an Ed.D. degree may be substituted for two years of the required experience. Preferred Qualifications: Ph.D. Three or more years of GIS experience Screening Information: Screening of applications begins immediately and will continue until the position is filled. How to Apply: To apply please visit https://employment.stockton.edu or click the \"Apply\" button. SAME APPLICANTS: If you are applying under the NJ “SAME” program, your supporting documents (Schedule A or B), must be submitted along with your resume by the closing date indicated above. For more information on the SAME Program visit their Website at https://www.nj.gov/csc/about/divisions/eeo/ email: CSC-Same@csc.nj.gov , or call 609-292-4144, option 3. In accordance with P.L. 2021, c. 465 and P.L. 2021, 466, the SAME Program was established to enable New Jersey State agencies to hire, promote, retain, and advance qualified individuals whose physical or mental impairments impact their abilities to participate in the hiring and promotion process for non-competitive and unclassified titles within the State workforce. This program uses a fast-track process that permits people who are eligible for the program to request that the State appointing authority schedule with them a good faith interview. Individuals applying for non-competitive or unclassified positions under this program should contact us to determine if they are eligible for the fast-track hiring process. Only electronic applications will be accepted. Please complete the online application and include the name, phone number and email of three professional references within the application in addition to the following required documents listed below. All required documents (Microsoft Word of PDF) must be submitted in order for your application to move forward. A letter of interest describing qualifications and accomplishments Current resume or curriculum vitae Unofficial Graduate transcripts #SU Please Be Advised : Stockton University is committed to providing every University employee and prospective University employee with a work environment free from prohibited discrimination or harassment. Prohibited discrimination or harassment undermines the integrity of the employment relationship, compromises equal employment opportunity, debilitates morale, and interferes with work productivity. Stockton University will not tolerate discrimination or harassment by anyone in our workplace including supervisors, co-workers, or persons doing business with our University. Stockton University is also committed to providing a learning, living, and working environment free from sexual misconduct. Sexual misconduct is a form of prohibited conduct that may constitute sex discrimination under Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, Titles IV and VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, the New Jersey Law Against Discrimination, and other applicable federal, state, and local laws, depending on the nature of the conduct and circumstances. To report concerns related to Discrimination, Harassment, and/or Sexual Misconduct/Title IX, please contact Joshua Hayes (Director of Title VI, Title VII & Title IX Coordinator – Office of Human Resources) via email at Joshua.Hayes@stockton.edu or by phone at (609) 652-4733. Persons with disabilities, who need reasonable accommodations to participate in the application and/or selection process, may contact Bart Musitano (ADA Coordinator and Manager for University Pensions and Benefits – Office of Human Resources) via email at Bart.Musitano@stockton.edu or by phone at (609) 652-4384. In accordance with the New Jersey First Act, P.L. 2011, c. 70, effective September 1, 2011, new public employees are required to establish New Jersey residency within one year of employment, unless they qualify for an applicable statutory or University-reported exemption. Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Campus Safety Act (Clery Act), prospective employees may access Stockton’s Annual Security and Fire Safety Report (ASFSR) at https://www.stockton.edu/police/crime-statistics.html . The ASFSR contains the previous three years of reported Clery Act crime statistics, fire safety information, and information regarding campus and personal safety. Paper copies of the report are available at our Stockton University Police Department located at 101 Vera King Farris Drive in Galloway, NJ - Building 70. To request a copy of the report be sent via postal mail, please send an email to campus.police@stockton.edu or call (609) 652-4390. Apply now! Sign up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 445c0676 Last Name (required) 667670a5 Email (required) dc356a9b Job Alert adc3a33b Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments School of Natural Sciences & Mathematics School of Natural Sciences & Mathematics Locations Port Republic, New Jersey, United States Port Republic, New Jersey, United States Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Share this job with a friend! First Name (required) 3e3a616d Last Name (required) 096600d2 Email (required) acb95c43 Share now Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you - we've sent an email with job to the person you entered. Apply Now! First Name (required) 3aa188d7 Last Name (required) c16afbb0 Email (required) 9b7fa90c Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Office of the President Read Stockton Now Media Resources Do Business With Stockton University Alerts Bookstore Library Employment Safety Information Statements & Policies Additional Locations Atlantic City Hammonton Manahawkin Stockton University 101 Vera King Farris Drive Galloway, NJ 08205-9441 (609) 652-1776 Maps, Directions & Parking Accessibility Statement Facebook Twitter YouTube Instagram LinkedIn Flickr Snapchat TikTok Stockton University is an Equal Opportunity Institution © 2022 Stockton University Candidate Details Please choose the location(s)"
