    "https://employment.stockton.edu/jobs/director-coastal-research-center-port-republic-new-jersey-united-states": {
      "title": "Director, Coastal Research Center",
      "description": "Director, Coastal Research Center - Port Republic, New Jersey, United States Director, Coastal Research Center - Port Republic, New Jersey, United States Kiosk mode Stockton University is ranked among the top public universities in the Northeast with more than 160 undergraduate and graduate programs, as well as continuing education opportunities. Our University, one hour from Philadelphia and two hours from New York City, offers unique learning, living, and working environments throughout southern New Jersey, including the 1,600-acre Galloway campus in the Pinelands National Reserve and Atlantic City campus, located in the University District, just steps from the beach and iconic Atlantic City Boardwalk. Additional locations include Hammonton and Manahawkin. As a public University, Stockton University provides an environment for excellence to our student body through an interdisciplinary approach to liberal arts, sciences, and professional education. Founded in 1969, our University held its first classes in 1971. Our University’s welcoming and vibrant community makes Stockton a great place to learn, live, and work! Learn more about the many reasons to choose Stockton at www.Stockton.edu . Our Faculty and Staff are committed to supporting Stockton University’s strong student-centered vision and mission. Director, Coastal Research Center Port Republic, New Jersey Port Republic - Coastal Research Center (CRC) Management Opened on: Oct 1 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Campus Location: Main Campus (Galloway) Department: School of Natural Sciences & Mathematics Salary Range: $125,000.00 - $138,580.00 Salary Information: NJ State employees are offered a full benefits package: medical, prescription drug, and dental coverage, paid time off, paid holidays, pension/retirement plan, supplemental retirement saving plan options, disability Insurance, and tax saving programs. University Pensions & Benefits Information Webpage Work Hours: Varies Brief Job Overview/Summary The Director of the Coastal Research Center (CRC) provides leadership for Stockton University's applied coastal research, securing funding and overseeing external projects, strategic partnerships, and CRC operations. Reporting to the Dean of the School of Natural Sciences and Mathematics (NAMS), the Director supports the University's academic mission through student engagement, collaboration with faculty, and contributions to teaching and research. The Director also serves as the CRC's primary representative to government agencies, clients, and other external partners, including the regional community and news organizations. This position is fully supported by sponsored research grants and contracts. Descriptions of Essential Duties/Responsibilities: Solicit and negotiate contracts reflecting the scope of work and financial arrangements with prospective clients and governmental agencies. Lead scientific research and scientific field studies by securing grant funding and collaborations and serving as the principal investigator and project manager. Recruit, train and supervise employees, providing guidance and leadership to enable them to complete operations and research within the CRC. Represent the University at meetings and engage with clients and federal, state, and municipal officials, providing information and expertise to support informed, science-based decision-making surrounding issues affecting New Jersey coastal communities. Provide materials to NAMS academic programs in Marine Science, Environmental Science, Geology, Sustainability and Coastal Zone Management. In coordination with the University Grants Office, oversees projects throughout the development, operational, and final reporting phases. Review and validate the data collection methodology and the means used to process it into tangible materials for CRC clients. Develop and review reports published on behalf of the CRC. Review project financial documentation to ensure accuracy and minimize processing errors. Complete other duties as assigned. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Knowledge of New Jersey coastal systems, coastal resilience, environmental policy, and resource management Written and verbal communication skills, including experience preparing scientific reports, technical documents, and presentations Experience developing and maintaining partnerships with government agencies, academic institutions, and external stakeholders Required Qualifications: Master's degree in marine science, coastal science, geology, environmental science, oceanography, engineering, hydrography, or a closely related field Five years of progressively responsible experience in applied research, coastal science, environmental consulting, or research administration Experience supervising professional staff and managing multidisciplinary research teams Preferred Qualifications: Doctoral degree in marine science, coastal science, geology, environmental science, oceanography, engineering, or a closely related field Experience directing a research center, institute, consulting organization, or similar applied research enterprise Experience securing, managing, and administering externally funded research projects and contracts, including oversight of project budgets and financial resources Screening Information: Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis by our Office of Human Resources beginning immediately and will continue until the position is filled. How to Apply: To apply please visit https://employment.stockton.edu or click the \"Apply\" button. Application Requirements: Individuals who apply must complete the online application, provide names and contact information for three professional references, and submit the following required documents electronically in a Microsoft Word or PDF format: Letter of Interest/Cover Letter Describing Qualifications and Accomplishments Current Resume, Vita, or Curriculum Vitae Unofficial Graduate transcripts Important: Individuals who apply must meet all Required Qualifications within the job advertisement to be considered for this position. Please note that any offer of employment is subject to, and contingent upon, completion of the University’s mandatory and favorable background check, which may include a consumer report, availability and receipt of appropriations from the State of New Jersey, and receipt of any required approvals by the University. SAME Program: In accordance with P.L. 2021, c. 465 and P.L. 2021, 466, the SAME Program permits eligible New Jersey State agencies and employers to consider qualified applicants for certain non-competitive and unclassified titles within the State workforce. Applicants seeking consideration under the New Jersey SAME Program, must indicate that status when completing the online application. You must also submit the required SAME Program documentation for this specific position, as directed by the New Jersey Civil Service Commission, in addition to all required electronic documents for this position (e.g., cover letter, resume/vita/curriculum vitae, unofficial transcripts) on or before the closing date indicated above. Individuals who apply through the SAME Program must meet all Required Qualifications within the job advertisement to be considered for this position. For more information on the SAME Program, please contact the New Jersey Civil Service Commission by emailing SAME@csc.nj.gov . #SU Please Be Advised : Stockton University is committed to providing every University employee and prospective University employee with a work environment free from prohibited discrimination or harassment. Prohibited discrimination or harassment undermines the integrity of the employment relationship, compromises equal employment opportunity, debilitates morale, and interferes with work productivity. Stockton University will not tolerate discrimination or harassment by anyone in our workplace including supervisors, co-workers, or persons doing business with our University. Stockton University is also committed to providing a learning, living, and working environment free from sexual misconduct. Sexual misconduct is a form of prohibited conduct that may constitute sex discrimination under Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, Titles IV and VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, the New Jersey Law Against Discrimination, and other applicable federal, state, and local laws, depending on the nature of the conduct and circumstances. To report concerns related to Discrimination, Harassment, and/or Sexual Misconduct/Title IX, please contact Joshua Hayes (Director of Title VI, Title VII & Title IX Coordinator – Office of Human Resources) via email at Joshua.Hayes@stockton.edu or by phone at (609) 652-4733. Persons with disabilities, who need reasonable accommodations to participate in the application and/or selection process, may contact Bart Musitano (ADA Coordinator and Manager for University Pensions and Benefits – Office of Human Resources) via email at Bart.Musitano@stockton.edu or by phone at (609) 652-4384. In accordance with the New Jersey First Act, P.L. 2011, c. 70, effective September 1, 2011, new public employees are required to establish New Jersey residency within one year of employment, unless they qualify for an applicable statutory or University-reported exemption. Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Campus Safety Act (Clery Act), prospective employees may access Stockton’s Annual Security and Fire Safety Report (ASFSR) at https://www.stockton.edu/police/crime-statistics.html . The ASFSR contains the previous three years of reported Clery Act crime statistics, fire safety information, and information regarding campus and personal safety. Paper copies of the report are available at our Stockton University Police Department located at 101 Vera King Farris Drive in Galloway, NJ - Building 70. To request a copy of the report be sent via postal mail, please send an email to campus.police@stockton.edu or call (609) 652-4390. Apply now! Sign up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 9bf30d55 Last Name (required) 35dfa023 Email (required) 467f21dd Job Alert 80dfeeb9 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments School of Natural Sciences & Mathematics School of Natural Sciences & Mathematics Locations Port Republic, New Jersey, United States Port Republic, New Jersey, United States Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Share this job with a friend! First Name (required) 20f5cfb2 Last Name (required) d65bd1a9 Email (required) 71c70354 Share now Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you - we've sent an email with job to the person you entered. Apply Now! First Name (required) f631fbc0 Last Name (required) d9e2419e Email (required) 1cf41943 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Office of the President Read Stockton Now Media Resources Do Business With Stockton University Alerts Bookstore Library Employment Safety Information Statements & Policies Additional Locations Atlantic City Hammonton Manahawkin Stockton University 101 Vera King Farris Drive Galloway, NJ 08205-9441 (609) 652-1776 Maps, Directions & Parking Accessibility Statement Facebook Twitter YouTube Instagram LinkedIn Flickr Snapchat TikTok Stockton University is an Equal Opportunity Institution © 2022 Stockton University Candidate Details Please choose the location(s)"
