    "https://employment.stockton.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-of-computer-information-systems-tenure-track-starting-09-01-2026-galloway-new-jersey-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Computer Information Systems, Tenure Track, Starting 09-01-2026",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Computer Information Systems, Tenure Track, Starting 09-01-2026 - Galloway, New Jersey, United States Assistant Professor of Computer Information Systems, Tenure Track, Starting 09-01-2026 - Galloway, New Jersey, United States Kiosk mode Stockton University is ranked among the top public universities in the Northeast with more than 160 undergraduate and graduate programs, as well as continuing education opportunities. Our University, one hour from Philadelphia and two hours from New York City, offers unique learning, living, and working environments throughout southern New Jersey, including the 1,600-acre Galloway campus in the Pinelands National Reserve and Atlantic City campus, located in the University District, just steps from the beach and iconic Atlantic City Boardwalk. Additional locations include Hammonton and Manahawkin. As a public University, Stockton University provides an environment for excellence to our student body through an interdisciplinary approach to liberal arts, sciences, and professional education. Founded in 1969, our University held its first classes in 1971. Our University’s welcoming and vibrant community makes Stockton a great place to learn, live, and work! Learn more about the many reasons to choose Stockton at www.Stockton.edu . Our Faculty and Staff are committed to supporting Stockton University’s strong student-centered vision and mission. Assistant Professor of Computer Information Systems, Tenure Track, Starting 09-01-2026 Galloway, New Jersey School of Business Faculty Full-time Opened on: Sep 15 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Campus Location: Main Campus (Galloway) Department: School of Business Salary: $76,486.40 - $99,422.70 Salary Information: NJ State employees are offered a full benefits package: medical, prescription drug, and dental coverage, paid time off, paid holidays, pension/retirement plan, supplemental retirement saving plan options, disability Insurance, and tax saving programs. University Pensions & Benefits Information Webpage Work Hours: Varies Brief Job Overview/Summary The AACSB accredited School of Business at Stockton University invites applications for two full-time tenure track Assistant Professor of Computer Information Systems starting September 1, 2024. Descriptions of Essential Duties/Responsibilities: The primary teaching responsibilities include teaching Computer Information Systems courses at the undergraduate and graduate levels. The program is specifically interested in candidates with expertise in teaching Advanced Databases, Machine Learning, Computer Networking, and System & Network Administration Preference will be given to candidates who demonstrate interest or have successful experience teaching courses such as Data Analytics, Data Visualization, Digital Forensics, Enterprise Resource Planning, Mobile & Web Application Programming All Stockton faculty members are required to teach courses in the University's interdisciplinary general studies program as well This position will most likely involve teaching at Stockton’s instructional sites in Galloway, NJ, and Atlantic City, NJ (approximately 12 miles apart) Along with building a track record of excellence in teaching, School of Business faculty members are expected to produce high-quality publications in scholarly journals and present peer-reviewed work at appropriate academic conferences Provide service to the University and community, as well as maintaining liaisons with appropriate professional groups and industry partners Support Stockton University’s diversity commitment and strong student-centered vision and mission Required Qualifications An earned doctorate in Computer Information Systems or a related discipline such as Information Systems, Management Information Systems, or Business Administration with an Information Systems concentration. Advanced ABDs will be considered, but hired as an Instructor until the degree is completed Preferred Qualifications: Evidence of potential for teaching, research, and service in Computer Information Systems or a related field Screening Information: Screening of applications begins immediately and will continue until the position is filled. How to Apply: To apply please visit https://employment.stockton.edu or click the \"Apply\" button. Only electronic documents will be accepted. Please complete the online application and include three professional references in addition to the following required documents. All required documents (Microsoft Word of PDF) must be submitted in order for your application to move forward. A letter of interest describing qualifications and accomplishments Current resume or curriculum vitae Unofficial Graduate transcripts Teaching philosophy statement (1 page) Documents showing evidence of teaching effectiveness Scholarship plans and research capabilities (1 page) #SU Please Be Advised : Stockton University is committed to providing every University employee and prospective University employee with a work environment free from prohibited discrimination or harassment. Prohibited discrimination or harassment undermines the integrity of the employment relationship, compromises equal employment opportunity, debilitates morale, and interferes with work productivity. Stockton University will not tolerate discrimination or harassment by anyone in our workplace including supervisors, co-workers, or persons doing business with our University. Stockton University is also committed to providing a learning, living, and working environment free from sexual misconduct. Sexual misconduct is a form of prohibited conduct that may constitute sex discrimination under Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, Titles IV and VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, the New Jersey Law Against Discrimination, and other applicable federal, state, and local laws, depending on the nature of the conduct and circumstances. To report concerns related to Discrimination, Harassment, and/or Sexual Misconduct/Title IX, please contact Joshua Hayes (Director of Title VI, Title VII & Title IX Coordinator – Office of Human Resources) via email at Joshua.Hayes@stockton.edu or by phone at (609) 652-4733. Persons with disabilities, who need reasonable accommodations to participate in the application and/or selection process, may contact Bart Musitano (ADA Coordinator and Manager for University Pensions and Benefits – Office of Human Resources) via email at Bart.Musitano@stockton.edu or by phone at (609) 652-4384. In accordance with the New Jersey First Act, P.L. 2011, c. 70, effective September 1, 2011, new public employees are required to establish New Jersey residency within one year of employment, unless they qualify for an applicable statutory or University-reported exemption. Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Campus Safety Act (Clery Act), prospective employees may access Stockton’s Annual Security and Fire Safety Report (ASFSR) at https://www.stockton.edu/police/crime-statistics.html . The ASFSR contains the previous three years of reported Clery Act crime statistics, fire safety information, and information regarding campus and personal safety. Paper copies of the report are available at our Stockton University Police Department located at 101 Vera King Farris Drive in Galloway, NJ - Building 70. To request a copy of the report be sent via postal mail, please send an email to campus.police@stockton.edu or call (609) 652-4390. Apply now! Sign up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 399edf52 Last Name (required) b5c428ef Email (required) 0c7c5799 Job Alert 50b5409f Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments School of Business School of Business Locations Galloway, New Jersey, United States Galloway, New Jersey, United States Send Please wait..