      "title": "TES - Men's Lacrosse Assistant Coach - Intercollegiate Sports",
      "description": "TES - Men's Lacrosse Assistant Coach - Intercollegiate Sports - Galloway, New Jersey, United States TES - Men's Lacrosse Assistant Coach - Intercollegiate Sports - Galloway, New Jersey, United States Kiosk mode Stockton University is ranked among the top public universities in the Northeast with more than 160 undergraduate and graduate programs, as well as continuing education opportunities. Our University, one hour from Philadelphia and two hours from New York City, offers unique learning, living, and working environments throughout southern New Jersey, including the 1,600-acre Galloway campus in the Pinelands National Reserve and Atlantic City campus, located in the University District, just steps from the beach and iconic Atlantic City Boardwalk. Additional locations include Hammonton and Manahawkin. As a public University, Stockton University provides an environment for excellence to our student body through an interdisciplinary approach to liberal arts, sciences, and professional education. Founded in 1969, our University held its first classes in 1971. Our University’s welcoming and vibrant community makes Stockton a great place to learn, live, and work! Learn more about the many reasons to choose Stockton at www.Stockton.edu . Our Faculty and Staff are committed to supporting Stockton University’s strong student-centered vision and mission. TES - Men's Lacrosse Assistant Coach - Intercollegiate Sports Galloway, New Jersey Athletics and Recreation Temporary (TES) Opened on: Aug 17 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Campus Location: Main Campus (Galloway) Department: Athletics & Campus Recreation Salary Information: Stipend Work Hours: Varies Brief Job Overview/Summary Under the direction of the Executive Director of Athletics and Campus Recreation, the Assistant Men's Lacrosse Coach is responsible for the following: • Assist in supervising all practice sessions and contests/competitions. • Assist in supervising and traveling with the team on trips. • Assist in maintaining the team's equipment and uniforms. • Assist in the recruitment of student athletes. • Maintain CPR Certification and annually complete the concussion training course. • Drive vehicles to transport students/staff on campus as well as to off campus events. • Adhere to the rules and regulations of the University, Athletic Office, National Collegiate Athletic Association, New Jersey Athletic Conference or affiliated conferences. • Comply with all medical decisions/protocols from Athletic Training Services. • Perform other duties assigned Descriptions of Essential Duties/Responsibilities: • Assist in supervising all practice sessions and contests/competitions. • Assist in supervising and traveling with the team on trips. • Assist in maintaining the team's equipment and uniforms. • Assist in the recruitment of student athletes. • Maintain CPR Certification and annually complete the concussion training course. • Drive vehicles to transport students/staff on campus as well as to off campus events. • Adhere to the rules and regulations of the University, Athletic Office, National Collegiate Athletic Association, New Jersey Athletic Conference or affiliated conferences. • Comply with all medical decisions/protocols from Athletic Training Services. • Perform other duties assigned Required Qualifications: • Bachelor's Degree • Minimum 1 year of coaching experience • Valid Driver's License Preferred Qualifications: • CPR Certification Screening Information: Screening of applications begins immediately and will continue until the position is filled. How to Apply: To apply please visit https://employment.stockton.edu or click the \"Apply\" button. Only electronic documents will be accepted. Please complete the online application and include three professional references in addition to the following required documents. All required documents (Microsoft Word of PDF) must be submitted in order for your application to move forward. A letter of interest describing qualifications and accomplishments Current resume Please Be Advised : Stockton University is committed to providing every University employee and prospective University employee with a work environment free from prohibited discrimination or harassment. Prohibited discrimination or harassment undermines the integrity of the employment relationship, compromises equal employment opportunity, debilitates morale, and interferes with work productivity. Stockton University will not tolerate discrimination or harassment by anyone in our workplace including supervisors, co-workers, or persons doing business with our University. Stockton University is also committed to providing a learning, living, and working environment free from sexual misconduct. Sexual misconduct is a form of prohibited conduct that may constitute sex discrimination under Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, Titles IV and VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, the New Jersey Law Against Discrimination, and other applicable federal, state, and local laws, depending on the nature of the conduct and circumstances. To report concerns related to Discrimination, Harassment, and/or Sexual Misconduct/Title IX, please contact Joshua Hayes (Director of Title VI, Title VII & Title IX Coordinator – Office of Human Resources) via email at Joshua.Hayes@stockton.edu or by phone at (609) 652-4733. Persons with disabilities, who need reasonable accommodations to participate in the application and/or selection process, may contact Bart Musitano (ADA Coordinator and Manager for University Pensions and Benefits – Office of Human Resources) via email at Bart.Musitano@stockton.edu or by phone at (609) 652-4384. In accordance with the New Jersey First Act, P.L. 2011, c. 70, effective September 1, 2011, new public employees are required to establish New Jersey residency within one year of employment, unless they qualify for an applicable statutory or University-reported exemption. Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Campus Safety Act (Clery Act), prospective employees may access Stockton’s Annual Security and Fire Safety Report (ASFSR) at https://www.stockton.edu/police/crime-statistics.html . The ASFSR contains the previous three years of reported Clery Act crime statistics, fire safety information, and information regarding campus and personal safety. Paper copies of the report are available at our Stockton University Police Department located at 101 Vera King Farris Drive in Galloway, NJ - Building 70. To request a copy of the report be sent via postal mail, please send an email to campus.police@stockton.edu or call (609) 652-4390. Apply now! Sign up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 8c23b7bb Last Name (required) 11a7e56f Email (required) d513b24c Job Alert 4b68ff1e Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Athletics & Campus Recreation Athletics & Campus Recreation Locations Galloway, New Jersey, United States Galloway, New Jersey, United States Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Share this job with a friend! First Name (required) 3bf0ec06 Last Name (required) 9d3986fd Email (required) 8bc2277c Share now Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you - we've sent an email with job to the person you entered. Apply Now! First Name (required) b1fb2134 Last Name (required) 6fd3cf60 Email (required) a7e14145 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Office of the President Read Stockton Now Media Resources Do Business With Stockton University Alerts Bookstore Library Employment Safety Information Statements & Policies Additional Locations Atlantic City Hammonton Manahawkin Stockton University 101 Vera King Farris Drive Galloway, NJ 08205-9441 (609) 652-1776 Maps, Directions & Parking Accessibility Statement Facebook Twitter YouTube Instagram