      "title": "Adjunct Faculty - School of Arts & Humanities, Visual Arts, Illustration",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty - School of Arts & Humanities, Visual Arts, Illustration - Galloway, New Jersey, United States Adjunct Faculty - School of Arts & Humanities, Visual Arts, Illustration - Galloway, New Jersey, United States Kiosk mode Stockton University is ranked among the top public universities in the Northeast with more than 160 undergraduate and graduate programs, as well as continuing education opportunities. Our University, one hour from Philadelphia and two hours from New York City, offers unique learning, living, and working environments throughout southern New Jersey, including the 1,600-acre Galloway campus in the Pinelands National Reserve and Atlantic City campus, located in the University District, just steps from the beach and iconic Atlantic City Boardwalk. Additional locations include Hammonton and Manahawkin. As a public University, Stockton University provides an environment for excellence to our student body through an interdisciplinary approach to liberal arts, sciences, and professional education. Founded in 1969, our University held its first classes in 1971. Our University’s welcoming and vibrant community makes Stockton a great place to learn, live, and work! Learn more about the many reasons to choose Stockton at www.Stockton.edu . Our Faculty and Staff are committed to supporting Stockton University’s strong student-centered vision and mission. Adjunct Faculty - School of Arts & Humanities, Visual Arts, Illustration Galloway, New Jersey School of Arts & Humanities Adjunct Faculty Opened on: Jun 2 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Campus Location: Main Campus (Galloway) Department: School of Arts and Humanities Salary Information: SFT Adjunct Rate $2,100 per credit Work Hours: Varies Brief Job Overview/Summary The School of Arts & Humanities is expanding its pool of qualified adjunct (part-time) instructors. Opportunities may exist to teach a flexible schedule that may include teaching assignments during days and evenings. Services are contracted on a semester/term basis. The Stockton University Visual Arts Program on Stockton Galloway campus seeks adjunct instructors to teach 2000 level Illustration 1 and 3000 level Illustration Practices courses. Classes are 2.5 hours and meet twice a week. Time slots Mondays and Wednesdays or Tuesdays and Thursdays, from 8:30 to 11:00, 11:20 to 1:50, 2:00 - 4:30 or 6:00pm-8:30pm. While all services are contracted on a semester/term basis, these courses are part of the core Visual Arts Curriculum, and successful candidates will be considered for ongoing and consistently scheduled teaching opportunities. Descriptions of Essential Duties/Responsibilities: Please visit the Stockton Visual Arts website (stockton.edu/arts-humanities/visual-arts) for additional information about our program and course offerings. Adjunct instructors are expected to: • Teach Undergraduate courses as scheduled • Access student work and provide timely feedback • Use Blackboard (the Learning Management System) to support the course • Support Stockton University’s strong student-centered vision and mission Required Qualifications: Bachelor of Fine Arts (BFA) or Bachelor (BA) Degree in related area Professional experience in related subject Preferred Qualifications: Master of Fine Arts (MFA) Screening Information: The job will be posted continuously to expand Stockton University’s pool of qualified Adjunct (part-time) instructors. Screening of applications are completed when open positions become available. How to Apply: To apply please visit https://employment.stockton.edu or click the \"Apply\" button. Only electronic applications will be accepted. Please complete the online application and include the name, phone number and email of three professional references within the application in addition to the following required documents listed below. All required documents (Microsoft Word of PDF) must be submitted in order for your application to move forward. A letter of interest describing qualifications and accomplishments Current resume or curriculum vitae Unofficial Graduate transcripts Please Be Advised : Stockton University is committed to providing every University employee and prospective University employee with a work environment free from prohibited discrimination or harassment. Prohibited discrimination or harassment undermines the integrity of the employment relationship, compromises equal employment opportunity, debilitates morale, and interferes with work productivity. Stockton University will not tolerate discrimination or harassment by anyone in our workplace including supervisors, co-workers, or persons doing business with our University. Stockton University is also committed to providing a learning, living, and working environment free from sexual misconduct. Sexual misconduct is a form of prohibited conduct that may constitute sex discrimination under Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, Titles IV and VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, the New Jersey Law Against Discrimination, and other applicable federal, state, and local laws, depending on the nature of the conduct and circumstances. To report concerns related to Discrimination, Harassment, and/or Sexual Misconduct/Title IX, please contact Joshua Hayes (Director of Title VI, Title VII & Title IX Coordinator – Office of Human Resources) via email at Joshua.Hayes@stockton.edu or by phone at (609) 652-4733. Persons with disabilities, who need reasonable accommodations to participate in the application and/or selection process, may contact Bart Musitano (ADA Coordinator and Manager for University Pensions and Benefits – Office of Human Resources) via email at Bart.Musitano@stockton.edu or by phone at (609) 652-4384. In accordance with the New Jersey First Act, P.L. 2011, c. 70, effective September 1, 2011, new public employees are required to establish New Jersey residency within one year of employment, unless they qualify for an applicable statutory or University-reported exemption. Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Campus Safety Act (Clery Act), prospective employees may access Stockton’s Annual Security and Fire Safety Report (ASFSR) at https://www.stockton.edu/police/crime-statistics.html . The ASFSR contains the previous three years of reported Clery Act crime statistics, fire safety information, and information regarding campus and personal safety. Paper copies of the report are available at our Stockton University Police Department located at 101 Vera King Farris Drive in Galloway, NJ - Building 70. To request a copy of the report be sent via postal mail, please send an email to campus.police@stockton.edu or call (609) 652-4390. Apply now! Sign up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 9485130d Last Name (required) be053af4 Email (required) 857f76d5 Job Alert b0bb1319 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments School of Arts and Humanities School of Arts and Humanities Locations Galloway, New Jersey, United States Galloway, New Jersey, United States Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Share this job with a friend! First Name (required) 51d0283f Last Name (required) fa516c4a Email (required) 7f5d3d97 Share now Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you - we've sent an email with job to the person you entered. Apply Now! First Name (required) 7fd57993 Last Name (required) d6e2cb2d Email (required) 9719fc2f Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Office of the President Read Stockton Now Media Resources Do Business With Stockton University Alerts Bookstore Library Employment Safety Information Statements & Policies Additional Locations Atlantic City Hammonton Manahawkin Stockton University 101 Vera King Farris Drive Galloway, NJ 08205-9441 (609) 652-1776 Maps, Directions & Parking Acce