ty of the employment relationship, compromises equal employment opportunity, debilitates morale, and interferes with work productivity. Stockton University will not tolerate discrimination or harassment by anyone in our workplace including supervisors, co-workers, or persons doing business with our University. Stockton University is also committed to providing a learning, living, and working environment free from sexual misconduct. Sexual misconduct is a form of prohibited conduct that may constitute sex discrimination under Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, Titles IV and VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, the New Jersey Law Against Discrimination, and other applicable federal, state, and local laws, depending on the nature of the conduct and circumstances. To report concerns related to Discrimination, Harassment, and/or Sexual Misconduct/Title IX, please contact Joshua Hayes (Director of Title VI, Title VII & Title IX Coordinator – Office of Human Resources) via email at Joshua.Hayes@stockton.edu or by phone at (609) 652-4733. Persons with disabilities, who need reasonable accommodations to participate in the application and/or selection process, may contact Bart Musitano (ADA Coordinator and Manager for University Pensions and Benefits – Office of Human Resources) via email at Bart.Musitano@stockton.edu or by phone at (609) 652-4384. In accordance with the New Jersey First Act, P.L. 2011, c. 70, effective September 1, 2011, new public employees are required to establish New Jersey residency within one year of employment, unless they qualify for an applicable statutory or University-reported exemption. Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Campus Safety Act (Clery Act), prospective employees may access Stockton’s Annual Security and Fire Safety Report (ASFSR) at https://www.stockton.edu/police/crime-statistics.html . The ASFSR contains the previous three years of reported Clery Act crime statistics, fire safety information, and information regarding campus and personal safety. Paper copies of the report are available at our Stockton University Police Department located at 101 Vera King Farris Drive in Galloway, NJ - Building 70. To request a copy of the report be sent via postal mail, please send an email to campus.police@stockton.edu or call (609) 652-4390. Apply now! Sign up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) e756c957 Last Name (required) 154aaeb7 Email (required) 75e62096 Job Alert 3d2f1dfd Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments School of Arts and Humanities School of Arts and Humanities Locations Galloway, New Jersey, United States Galloway, New Jersey, United States Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Share this job with a friend! First Name (required) cfd34e76 Last Name (required) bc195145 Email (required) 83b96c38 Share now Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you - we've sent an email with job to the person you entered. Apply Now! First Name (required) 71e1f05d Last Name (required) 7ff9e7b3 Email (required) d1568fa3 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Office of the President Read Stockton Now Media Resources Do Business With Stockton University Alerts Bookstore Library Employment Safety Information Statements & Policies Additional Locations Atlantic City Hammonton Manahawkin Stockton University 101 Vera King Farris Drive Galloway, NJ 08205-9441 (609) 652-1776 Maps, Directions & Parking Accessibility Statement Facebook Twitter YouTube Instagram LinkedIn Flickr Snapchat TikTok Stockton University is an Equal Opportunity Institution © 2022 Stockton University Candidate Details Please choose the location(s)"
