s expanding its pool of qualified adjunct (part-time) instructors. Opportunities may exist to teach a flexible schedule that may include teaching assignments during days and evenings. Services are contracted on a semester/term basis. The Communication Studies program is seeking adjuncts in the following areas of specialization(s): Public Relations & Advertising, Media Production, and Journalism and Community Storytelling. The preferred candidates(s) will have a minimum of a Master's degree in their respective area of expertise, significant professional expertise and be current in their fields of study. The job will be posted continuously to expand Stockton University’s pool of qualified Adjunct (part-time) instructors. Screening of applications are completed when open positions become available. Descriptions of Essential Duties/Responsibilities: Please visit the Stockton Communication Studies website for additional information about our program and course offerings. Adjunct instructors are expected to: Teach Undergraduate courses as scheduled Access student work and provide timely feedback Use Blackboard (the Learning Management System) to support the course Support Stockton University’s strong student-centered vision and mission Required Qualifications A minimum of a Master's degree in their respective area of expertise, significant professional expertise and be current in their fields of study Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Knowledge of current editing software a must, Adobe Premiere and the Adobe Creative Suite as well as current knowledge and experience with professional DSLR and field production cameras, lighting, and audio equipment Knowledge and experience using MAC computers required Screening Information: The job will be posted continuously to expand Stockton University’s pool of qualified Adjunct (part-time) instructors. Screening of applications are completed when open positions become available. How to Apply: To apply please visit https://employment.st