    "https://employment.stockton.edu/jobs/assistant-vice-president-for-enrollment-management-galloway-new-jersey-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant Vice President for Enrollment Management",
      "description": "Assistant Vice President for Enrollment Management - Galloway, New Jersey, United States Assistant Vice President for Enrollment Management - Galloway, New Jersey, United States Kiosk mode Stockton University is ranked among the top public universities in the Northeast with more than 160 undergraduate and graduate programs, as well as continuing education opportunities. Our University, one hour from Philadelphia and two hours from New York City, offers unique learning, living, and working environments throughout southern New Jersey, including the 1,600-acre Galloway campus in the Pinelands National Reserve and Atlantic City campus, located in the University District, just steps from the beach and iconic Atlantic City Boardwalk. Additional locations include Hammonton and Manahawkin. As a public University, Stockton University provides an environment for excellence to our student body through an interdisciplinary approach to liberal arts, sciences, and professional education. Founded in 1969, our University held its first classes in 1971. Our University’s welcoming and vibrant community makes Stockton a great place to learn, live, and work! Learn more about the many reasons to choose Stockton at www.Stockton.edu . Our Faculty and Staff are committed to supporting Stockton University’s strong student-centered vision and mission. Assistant Vice President for Enrollment Management Galloway, New Jersey Enrollment Management Management Opened on: Oct 21 2026 Campus Location: Main Campus (Galloway) Department: VPEM Administration Salary Range: $140,000 - $145,000 Salary Information: NJ State employees are offered a full benefits package: medical, prescription drug, and dental coverage, paid time off, paid holidays, pension/retirement plan, supplemental retirement saving plan options, disability Insurance, and tax saving programs. University Pensions & Benefits Information Webpage Work Hours: M-F 9am-5pm Brief Job Overview/Summary Reporting to the Vice President for Enrollment Management, the Assistant Vice President (AVP) for Enrollment Management provides strategic and operational leadership for undergraduate recruitment, admissions, transfer, and dual credit initiatives to support the University's enrollment goals and Strategic Enrollment Management Plan. The position oversees admissions, dual credit, and transfer operations; develops recruitment, enrollment, and yield strategies; uses enrollment data and market intelligence to make informed decisions; and collaborates with Academic Affairs, Student Affairs, and other campus partners to advance enrollment, retention, and student success priorities. As a member of the Enrollment Management leadership team, the AVP represents the University with external constituencies and serves as the Vice President's designee as assigned. Descriptions of Essential Duties/Responsibilities: Lead, supervise, develop, and evaluate admissions, dual credit, and transfer leadership staff; establish performance expectations and accountability; promote professional development; and foster a collaborative, student-centered culture aligned with the University's Ethic of Care. Assist the VP for Enrollment Management in providing strategic and operational leadership for Enrollment Management functions. Establish and monitor recruitment, enrollment, persistence, and retention goals, strategies, performance measures, and timelines aligned with the Strategic Enrollment Management Plan. Oversee the development, implementation, and assessment of undergraduate recruitment, admissions, transfer, dual credit, communication, conversion, and yield strategies to support enrollment goals. Lead transfer enrollment initiatives and strengthen community college partnerships in collaboration with Academic Affairs. Analyze and assess enrollment, market, student, and CRM data to identify trends, opportunities, and risks; forecast enrollment; evaluate performance; and inform recruitment strategies, resource allocation, and operational decision-making. Work collaboratively with the VP for Enrollment Management and divisional leadership, to develop and maintain partnerships with high schools, school districts, community organizations, community colleges, and other external stakeholders to advance recruitment, transfer, and enrollment initiatives. Represent the University at recruitment events. Collaborate with the VP for Enrollment Management, Academic Affairs, Student Affairs, University Relations and Marketing, Financial Aid, Institutional Research and Effectiveness, Athletics, and other campus partners to align enrollment, student success, retention, and academic programs. Assist the VP for Enrollment Management to ensure the codification, optimization, and continuous improvement of enrollment management and dual credit policies, procedures, technologies, communications, and service standards. Leverage CRM and enrollment technologies to enhance efficiency, communication, data integrity, and the prospective student experience. Represent the Division of Enrollment Management and the University in internal and external forums; prepare enrollment reports and recommendations for University leadership; serve as the Vice President's designee. Perform other duties as assigned. Required Qualifications: Master's degree in higher education administration, enrollment management, educational leadership, business administration, or a related field from an accredited institution. Five years of progressively responsible full-time work experience in higher education enrollment management, admissions, transfer, recruitment, or a closely related area, including supervisory or management responsibility. Possession of a valid driver's license and ability to travel regularly within assigned recruitment territories. Preferred Qualifications: Experience with Slate or a comparable customer relationship management (CRM) system. Experience working in a collective bargaining environment. Screening Information: Screening of applications begins immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Applications received or or before Tuesday, November 24, 2026, will receive full consideration. How to Apply: To apply please visit https://employment.stockton.edu or click the \"Apply\" button. Application Requirements: Individuals who apply must complete the online application, provide names and contact information for three professional references, and submit the following required documents electronically in a Microsoft Word or PDF format: Letter of Interest/Cover Letter Describing Qualifications and Accomplishments Current Resume, Vita, or Curriculum Vitae Unofficial Graduate transcripts Important: Individuals who apply must meet all Required Qualifications within the job advertisement to be considered for this position. Please note that any offer of employment is subject to, and contingent upon, completion of the University’s mandatory and favorable background check, which may include a consumer report, availability and receipt of appropriations from the State of New Jersey, and receipt of any required approvals by the University. SAME Program: In accordance with P.L. 2021, c. 465 and P.L. 2021, 466, the SAME Program permits eligible New Jersey State agencies and employers to consider qualified applicants for certain non-competitive and unclassified titles within the State workforce. Applicants seeking consideration under the New Jersey SAME Program, must indicate that status when completing the online application. You must also submit the required SAME Program documentation for this specific position, as directed by the New Jersey Civil Service Commission, in addition to all required electronic documents for this position (e.g., cover letter, resume/vita/curriculum vitae, unofficial transcripts) on or before the closing date indicated above. Individuals who apply through the SAME Program must meet all Required Qualifications within the job advertisement to be considered for this position. For more information on the SAME Program, please contact the New Jersey Civil Service Commission by emailing SAME@csc.nj.gov . #SU Please Be Advised : Stockton University does not discriminate in its application process, employment, educational programs and activities on the basis of race, creed, color, national origin, nationality, ancestry, age, sex/gender, pregnancy, marital status, civil union status, domestic partnership status, familial status, religion, affectional or sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, atypical hereditary cellular or blood trait , genetic information, liability for service in the Armed Forces of the United States, or disability, including perceived disability, physical, mental and/or intellectual disabilities. Stockton University is committed to providing every University employee and prospective University employee with a work environment free from prohibited discrimination or harassment. Prohibited discrimination or harassment undermines the integrity of the employment relationship, compromises equal employment opportunity, debilitates morale, and interferes with work productivity. Stockton University will not tolerate discrimination or harassment by anyone in our workplace including supervisors, co-workers, or persons doing business with our University. Stockton University is also committed to providing a learning, living, and working environment free from sexual misconduct. Sexual misconduct is a form of prohibited conduct that may constitute sex discrimination under Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, Titles IV and VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, the New Jersey Law Against Discrimination, and other applicable federal, state, and local laws, depending on the nature of the conduct and circumstances. To report concerns related to Discrimination, Harassment, and/or Sexual Misconduct/Title IX, please contact Joshua Hayes (Director of Title VI, Title VII & Title IX Coordinator – Office of Human Resources) via email at Joshua.Hayes@stockton.edu or by phone at (609) 652-4733. Persons with disabilities, who need reasonable accommodations to participate in the application and/or selection process, may contact Bart Musitano (ADA Coordinator and Manager for University Pensions and Benefits – Office of Human Resources) via email at Bart.Musitano@stockton.edu or by phone at (609) 652-4384. In accordance with the New Jersey First Act, P.L. 2011, c. 70, effective September 1, 2011, new public employees are required to establish New Jersey residency within one year of employment, unless they qualify for an applicable statutory or University-reported exemption. Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Campus Safety Act (Clery Act), prospective employees may access Stockton’s Annual Security and Fire Safety Report (ASFSR) at https://www.stockton.edu/police/crime-statistics.html . The ASFSR contains the previous three years of reported Clery Act crime statistics, fire safety information, and information regarding campus and personal safety. Paper copies of the report are available at our Stockton University Police Department located at 101 Vera King Farris Drive in Galloway, NJ - Building 70. To request a copy of the report be sent via postal mail, please send an email to campus.police@stockton.edu or call (609) 652-4390. Apply now! Sign up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 2302b937 Last Name (required) c7f85bf4 Email (required) fc9730ea Job Alert 6959edd5 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments VPEM Administration VPEM Administration Locations Galloway, New Jersey, United States Galloway, New Jersey, United States Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Share this job with a friend! First Name (required) 4f8785a4 Last Name (required) cf956cc3 Email (required) 6cf311db Share now Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you - we've sent an email with job to the person you entered. Apply Now! First Name (required) 2ddf1423 Last Name (required) 56e4dd8c Email (required) b7f0a37e Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Office of the President Read Stockton Now Media Resources Do Business With Stockton University Alerts Bookstore Library Employment Safety Information Statements & Policies Additional Locations Atlantic City Hammonton Manahawkin Stockton University 101 Vera King Farris Drive Galloway, NJ 08205-9441 (609) 652-1776 Maps, Directions & Parking Accessibility Statement Facebook Twitter YouTube Instagram LinkedIn Flickr Snapchat TikTok Stockton University is an Equal Opportunity Institution © 2022 Stockton University Candidate Details Please choose the location(s)"
