    "https://employment.stockton.edu/jobs/associate-dean-school-of-education-galloway-new-jersey-united-states": {
      "title": "Associate Dean, School of Education",
      "description": "Associate Dean, School of Education - Galloway, New Jersey, United States Associate Dean, School of Education - Galloway, New Jersey, United States Kiosk mode Stockton University is ranked among the top public universities in the Northeast with more than 160 undergraduate and graduate programs, as well as continuing education opportunities. Our University, one hour from Philadelphia and two hours from New York City, offers unique learning, living, and working environments throughout southern New Jersey, including the 1,600-acre Galloway campus in the Pinelands National Reserve and Atlantic City campus, located in the University District, just steps from the beach and iconic Atlantic City Boardwalk. Additional locations include Hammonton and Manahawkin. As a public University, Stockton University provides an environment for excellence to our student body through an interdisciplinary approach to liberal arts, sciences, and professional education. Founded in 1969, our University held its first classes in 1971. Our University’s welcoming and vibrant community makes Stockton a great place to learn, live, and work! Learn more about the many reasons to choose Stockton at www.Stockton.edu . Our Faculty and Staff are committed to supporting Stockton University’s strong student-centered vision and mission. Associate Dean, School of Education Galloway, New Jersey School of Education Management Opened on: Oct 20 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Campus Location: Main Campus (Galloway) Department: School of Education Salary Range: $130,000 - $140,000 Salary Information: Salary commensurate with experience and is accompanied by an extremely competitive University benefits package University Pensions & Benefits Information Webpage Work Hours: Mon. - Fri. 9:00am - 5:00pm Brief Job Overview/Summary Reporting to the Dean of Education, the Associate Dean of Education serves as a key partner in advancing the School of Education’s academic, fiscal, and administrative priorities. The Associate Dean collaborates with the Dean to provide strategic leadership in curriculum and program development, accreditation and program review, assessment, faculty and staff recruitment and retention, and the advancement of research, scholarship, and grant activity. The Associate Dean also supports fundraising efforts and represents the School to senior administration, students, alumni, and internal and external constituents, alongside, and at the discretion of the Dean. Descriptions of Essential Duties/Responsibilities: Academic Leadership: Collaborates with the Dean to provide innovative leadership and vision in the development, growth, and implementation of academic programs and policies within the School. Provides guidance on program planning, evaluation, curriculum development, and the assessment of student learning outcomes to promote continuous improvement. Working in collaboration with Chairs and the Office of Assessment, the Associate Dean collaborates to review programs, processes and recommends enhancements to academic offerings, including the integration of emerging technologies, in collaboration with the Dean. Ensures the achievement of strategic plan goals aligned with the School’s priorities as established by the Dean. Supports compliance with state and regional accreditation standards and specialized accreditation requirements for applicable programs. Promotes the expansion and quality of in-person, hybrid, and online programs, dual credit opportunities, and other innovative instructional initiatives. Faculty, Staff, and Student Success: Supports the recruitment, development, and retention of excellent full-time faculty, adjunct faculty, and professional staff. Fosters an inclusive academic environment that emphasizes professionalism, excellence, integrity, and collaboration. Supports strategic enrollment initiatives, including student recruitment and retention, program marketing, and community engagement. Manages the resolution of student concerns related to instruction, grades, program requirements, and course scheduling. Assists in the training, mentoring, and professional development of School staff. Advances a scholarly environment aligned with the University's mission, values, and strategic priorities while enhancing the visibility and impact of the School’s educational, outreach, and research activities. Operations and Administration: Assists the Dean and staff in developing and managing the School’s operating budget; supports resource planning, allocation, and expenditures. Maintains clear lines of communication among faculty, chairs, staff, students, and administrators to promote a collegial and supportive working and learning environment. In collaboration with the Dean, monitors School’s facilities to ensure offices, classrooms, and laboratories provide a safe, user-friendly environment for all occupants. Ensures compliance with state and federal regulations and University policies. External Relations and Institutional Engagement: Serves as an active member of the Deans Council and represents the Dean in University-wide and School-wide meetings, committees, and leadership initiatives upon Dean’s request or absence. Partners with the Dean and Institutional Advancement to support fundraising initiatives that sustain programs and secure funding for scholarships, technology, and capital priorities, while encouraging public-private partnerships. Maintains productive relationships with alumni, donors, community leaders, and other stakeholders to support strategic improvement efforts. Represents the School of Education and the University at state and national meetings, conferences, and events. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Collaborative leadership skills with the ability to foster inclusive, high-performing teams and working relationships. Ability to communicate in an interpersonal, written, and oral manner across a complex academic community. Strategic thinking, analytical ability, and sound judgment in addressing complex organizational challenges. Ability to mentor, develop, and empower faculty and staff while promoting a culture of accountability and continuous improvement. Experience in programmatic accreditation. Experience in fundraising and working with development and foundation teams. Experience securing and managing all components of grant funding, including proposal development, project development, team leadership, and grant administration. Ability to establish and sustain external partnerships with community stakeholders and organizations. Experience supporting student success. Ability to work in technology-rich environments, including support for online and hybrid education. Commitment to inclusive and academic excellence. Required Qualifications: Earned doctorate from an accredited institution in a discipline aligned with the School’s academic programs. Five years of full-time teaching experience at a college or university, with a strong record of scholarship and service commensurate with the rank of Associate or Full Professor. Three years of progressively responsible administrative or faculty leadership experience, including engagement with strategic enrollment initiatives and student success efforts. Experience as a teacher and/or administrator in a P–12 setting, with demonstrated expertise in state licensure and regulatory requirements. Experience working in technology-rich environments, including support for online and hybrid education. Preferred Qualifications: Demonstrated experience with recruitment and retention efforts. Engaged in and led significant work in programmatic accreditation. Experienced in fund raising and working with development and foundation teams. Experienced in all components of grant funding, from NGO, writing, project development, team building and leading, through directorship. Experienced identifying, building, and fostering external relations with community stakeholders and partners. Screening Information: Screening of applications begins immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Applications received by (insert date below in Job Posting after clicking Generate Description) will receive full consideration. How to Apply: To apply please visit https://employment.stockton.edu or click the \"Apply\" button. Application Requirements: Individuals who apply must complete the online application, provide names and contact information for three professional references, and submit the following required documents electronically in a Microsoft Word or PDF format: Letter of Interest/Cover Letter Describing Qualifications and Accomplishments Current Resume, Vita, or Curriculum Vitae Unofficial Graduate transcripts Important: Individuals who apply must meet all Required Qualifications within the job advertisement to be considered for this position. Please note that any offer of employment is subject to, and contingent upon, completion of the University’s mandatory and favorable background check, which may include a consumer report, availability and receipt of appropriations from the State of New Jersey, and receipt of any required approvals by the University. SAME Program: In accordance with P.L. 2021, c. 465 and P.L. 2021, 466, the SAME Program permits eligible New Jersey State agencies and employers to consider qualified applicants for certain non-competitive and unclassified titles within the State workforce. Applicants seeking consideration under the New Jersey SAME Program, must indicate that status when completing the online application. You must also submit the required SAME Program documentation for this specific position, as directed by the New Jersey Civil Service Commission, in addition to all required electronic documents for this position (e.g., cover letter, resume/vita/curriculum vitae, unofficial transcripts) on or before the closing date indicated above. Individuals who apply through the SAME Program must meet all Required Qualifications within the job advertisement to be considered for this position. For more information on the SAME Program, please contact the New Jersey Civil Service Commission by emailing SAME@csc.nj.gov . #SU Please Be Advised : Stockton University does not discriminate in its application process, employment, educational programs and activities on the basis of race, creed, color, national origin, nationality, ancestry, age, sex/gender, pregnancy, marital status, civil union status, domestic partnership status, familial status, religion, affectional or sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, atypical hereditary cellular or blood trait , genetic information, liability for service in the Armed Forces of the United States, or disability, including perceived disability, physical, mental and/or intellectual disabilities. Stockton University is committed to providing every University employee and prospective University employee with a work environment free from prohibited discrimination or harassment. Prohibited discrimination or harassment undermines the integrity of the employment relationship, compromises equal employment opportunity, debilitates morale, and interferes with work productivity. Stockton University will not tolerate discrimination or harassment by anyone in our workplace including supervisors, co-workers, or persons doing business with our University. Stockton University is also committed to providing a learning, living, and working environment free from sexual misconduct. Sexual misconduct is a form of prohibited conduct that may constitute sex discrimination under Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, Titles IV and VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, the New Jersey Law Against Discrimination, and other applicable federal, state, and local laws, depending on the nature of the conduct and circumstances. To report concerns related to Discrimination, Harassment, and/or Sexual Misconduct/Title IX, please contact Joshua Hayes (Director of Title VI, Title VII & Title IX Coordinator – Office of Human Resources) via email at Joshua.Hayes@stockton.edu or by phone at (609) 652-4733. Persons with disabilities, who need reasonable accommodations to participate in the application and/or selection process, may contact Bart Musitano (ADA Coordinator and Manager for University Pensions and Benefits – Office of Human Resources) via email at Bart.Musitano@stockton.edu or by phone at (609) 652-4384. In accordance with the New Jersey First Act, P.L. 2011, c. 70, effective September 1, 2011, new public employees are required to establish New Jersey residency within one year of employment, unless they qualify for an applicable statutory or University-reported exemption. Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Campus Safety Act (Clery Act), prospective employees may access Stockton’s Annual Security and Fire Safety Report (ASFSR) at https://www.stockton.edu/police/crime-statistics.html . The ASFSR contains the previous three years of reported Clery Act crime statistics, fire safety information, and information regarding campus and personal safety. Paper copies of the report are available at our Stockton University Police Department located at 101 Vera King Farris Drive in Galloway, NJ - Building 70. To request a copy of the report be sent via postal mail, please send an email to campus.police@stockton.edu or call (609) 652-4390. Apply now! Sign up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 788525ac Last Name (required) daac6e1d Email (required) cd63ca5d Job Alert a722a4b5 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments School of Education School of Education Locations Galloway, New Jersey, United States Galloway, New Jersey, United States Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Share this job with a friend! First Name (required) 2de469dc Last Name (required) bf808c5f Email (required) e59b2e21 Share now Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you - we've sent an email with job to the person you entered. Apply Now! First Name (required) cc004f04 Last Name (required) c5e97c50 Email (required) 210270e4 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Office of the President Read Stockton Now Media Resources Do Business With Stockton University Alerts Bookstore Library Employment Safety Information Statements & Policies Additional Locations Atlantic City Hammonton Manahawkin Stockton University 101 Vera King Farris Drive Galloway, NJ 08205-9441 (609) 652-1776 Maps, Directions & Parking Accessibility Statement Facebook Twitter YouTube Instagram LinkedIn Flickr Snapchat TikTok Stockton University is an Equal Opportunity Institution © 2022 Stockton University Candidate Details Please choose the location(s)"
